.\" linkmarks.1 — manual page for the LinkMarks CLI (Fase 2).
.\"
.\" Plain roff, -man macros. No pandoc, no asciidoctor. Keep it portable.
.\" Render with: man -l docs/man/linkmarks.1
.\"              groff -man -Tutf8 docs/man/linkmarks.1

.TH LINKMARKS 1 "2026-08-05" "LinkMarks 1.0.0" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
linkmarks \- local\-first, deterministic bookmark manager

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linkmarks
[\fIGLOBAL\-OPTIONS\fR] \fICommand\fR [\fICOMMAND\-OPTIONS\fR] [\fIARGS\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B linkmarks
imports, deduplicates, lists, and exports browser bookmarks without
phoning home or requiring a server.
It is a single static binary that follows the XDG Base Directory
specification and stores data in a local SQLite database under WAL mode.

The CLI has two layers:

.TP
.B Global options
apply to every subcommand. They control output format (\fB\-\-format\fR),
verbosity (\fB\-v\fR / \fB\-vv\fR), and the location of the SQLite store
(\fB\-\-store\fR) and the TOML config file (\fB\-\-config\fR).

.TP
.B Subcommands
each have their own scope and arguments. See
.B SUBCOMMANDS
below.

.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-format \fIFMT\fR
Output format for the active command. One of
.BR table " (default), " json ", or " yaml .
.TP
.B \-v
Increase verbosity (info).
Use twice (\fB\-vv\fR) for debug.
.TP
.B \-\-store \fIPATH\fR
Override the SQLite store path. Defaults to the XDG data dir.
May also be set via the \fBLINKMARKS_STORE\fR environment variable.
.TP
.B \-\-config \fIPATH\fR
Override the config file path. Defaults to the XDG config dir.
May also be set via the \fBLINKMARKS_CONFIG\fR environment variable.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print the global help text and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version string and exit.

.SH SUBCOMMANDS

.SS linkmarks init
Initialize the LinkMarks store and config directories.

Creates the XDG data and config directories, writes a default
\fBconfig.toml\fR if none is present, and opens the SQLite store
(which stamps \fBPRAGMA user_version\fR after running the migrator).

.RS
.nf
\fBUsage:\fR  linkmarks init [\-\-data\-dir \fIPATH\fR] [\-\-config\-dir \fIPATH\fR] [\-\-force]
.fi

.TP
.B \-\-data\-dir \fIPATH\fR
Override the data directory (defaults to XDG).
.TP
.B \-\-config\-dir \fIPATH\fR
Override the config directory (defaults to XDG).
.TP
.B \-\-force
Overwrite an existing \fBconfig.toml\fR with the bundled defaults.
Off by default. When the file is overwritten, the previous version
is renamed to \fBconfig.toml.bak\fR.
.RE

.SS linkmarks list
List bookmarks from a source or from the local store.

.RS
.nf
\fBUsage:\fR  linkmarks list [\-\-source \fINAME\fR] [\-\-path \fIPATH\fR] \\
                 [\-\-limit \fIN\fR] [\-\-offset \fIN\fR]
.fi

.TP
.B \-\-source \fINAME\fR
Source to list from. One of:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fBstore\fR \(em read from the SQLite store (default once the store exists).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBchrome\fR \(em parse a Chromium-family \fBBookmarks\fR JSON file.
.RE
.TP
.B \-\-path \fIPATH\fR
Path to a source file. Required when \fB\-\-source=chrome\fR; otherwise
the OS-typical Chrome path is used.
.TP
.B \-\-limit \fIN\fR
Maximum rows to print (store source). Default: \fB100\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-offset \fIN\fR
Row offset for pagination. Default: \fB0\fR.
.RE

.SS linkmarks import
Import bookmarks from a source file into the local store.

.RS
.nf
\fBUsage:\fR  linkmarks import \-\-source \fINAME\fR \-\-path \fIPATH\fR \\
                 [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-fresh]
.fi

.TP
.B \-\-source \fINAME\fR
Source to import from. Currently \fBchrome\fR is supported
(also covers Brave, Edge, Arc, Vivaldi, Opera).
.TP
.B \-\-path \fIPATH\fR
Path to the source file.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Parse and canonicalize but do not write the store.
.TP
.B \-\-fresh
Overwrite the destination store with a fresh DB.
Mutually exclusive with \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR.
.RE

.SS linkmarks export
Export bookmarks to a sink format.

.RS
.nf
\fBUsage:\fR  linkmarks export [\-\-format \fINAME\fR] [\-\-source \fINAME\fR] \\
                 [\-\-path \fIPATH\fR] [\-o, \-\-output \fIPATH\fR]
.fi

.TP
.B \-\-format \fINAME\fR
Output format. One of:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fBnetscape\fR (default) \(em emit a Netscape bookmark HTML file.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBjson\fR \(em emit NDJSON, one bookmark per line.
.RE
.TP
.B \-\-source \fINAME\fR
Source to export from. One of \fBstore\fR (default) or \fBchrome\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-output \fIPATH\fR
Output path. Use \fB\-\fR to write to stdout. Default: \fB\-\fR.
.RE

.SS linkmarks dedupe
Dedupe by canonical URL with a human-readable conflict report.

.RS
.nf
\fBUsage:\fR  linkmarks dedupe [\-\-source \fINAME\fR] [\-\-path \fIPATH\fR] \\
                 [\-\-apply] [\-\-refresh\-canonical]
.fi

.TP
.B \-\-source \fINAME\fR
Source to dedupe. \fBstore\fR (default) reads the SQLite store;
\fBchrome\fR parses a Chromium JSON file.
.TP
.B \-\-path \fIPATH\fR
Path to a Chromium JSON source. Required for \fB\-\-source=chrome\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-apply
Apply the merge. Without this flag, the command is dry-run only
and only reports conflicts.
.TP
.B \-\-refresh\-canonical
Recompute \fBcanonical_url\fR on every row by re-running the loader
config. Useful after editing \fBconfig.toml\fR to tighten rules.
.RE

.SS linkmarks tui
Launch the interactive terminal browser.

.RS
.nf
\fBUsage:\fR  linkmarks tui [\-\-source \fINAME\fR] \\
                 [\-\-netscape\-path \fIPATH\fR] \\
                 [\-\-chromium\-path \fIPATH\fR]
.fi

The TUI presents three panes: a bookmark list (left), a detail pane
(right), and a status bar (bottom). Vim-like bindings are supported
(\fBj\fR / \fBk\fR / \fBg\fR / \fBG\fR / \fB?\fR / \fBq\fR / \fBEnter\fR / \fBr\fR)
in addition to arrow keys, \fBPgUp\fR/\fBPgDn\fR, and \fBCtrl\-C\fR.

Substring filter mode is toggled with \fB/\fR; \fBEsc\fR clears,
\fBEnter\fR accepts.

.TP
.B \-\-source \fINAME\fR
Source selection. One of:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fBall\fR (default) \(em merge every available source and dedupe by canonical URL.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBchrome\fR, \fBnetscape\fR, \fBfirefox\fR \(em restrict to that source only.
.RE
.TP
.B \-\-netscape\-path \fIPATH\fR
Override the Netscape HTML path used by the TUI source registry.
.TP
.B \-\-chromium\-path \fIPATH\fR
Override the Chromium \fBBookmarks\fR JSON path used by the TUI source registry.
.RE

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Partial success or source error.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments.
.TP
.B 3
Dedupe conflicts found (non-fatal; review the report).

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LINKMARKS_STORE
Override the path to the SQLite store.
Equivalent to \fB\-\-store\fR.
.TP
.B LINKMARKS_CONFIG
Override the path to the TOML config file.
Equivalent to \fB\-\-config\fR.
.TP
.B LINKMARKS_TUI_DEFAULT_SOURCE
Default \fB\-\-source\fR value for \fBlinkmarks tui\fR.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Standard \fBtracing\fR filter. Honoured on stderr. Default:
\fBlinkmarks=warn,warn\fR. Try \fBRUST_LOG=linkmarks=debug\fR for verbose tracing.

.SH FILES
Paths follow the XDG Base Directory specification.

.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/linkmarks/store.db
SQLite store (default:
.BR $HOME/.local/share/linkmarks/store.db ).
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/linkmarks/config.toml
TOML config (default:
.BR $HOME/.config/linkmarks/config.toml ).
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/linkmarks/config.toml.bak
Backup of the previous config written by \fBlinkmarks init \-\-force\fR.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/man/man1/linkmarks.1
System manpage once installed by the system packager (not managed
by \fBscripts/install.sh\fR).

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B Initialize the local store with XDG defaults
.PP
.RS
.nf
linkmarks init
.fi
.RE

.TP
.B Import a Chromium Bookmarks JSON file
.PP
.RS
.nf
linkmarks import \-\-source=chrome \\
    \-\-path ~/.config/google-chrome/Default/Bookmarks
.fi
.RE

.TP
.B List bookmarks from the local store as JSON
.PP
.RS
.nf
linkmarks list \-\-source=store \-\-format=json
.fi
.RE

.TP
.B Export to a Netscape HTML file
.PP
.RS
.nf
linkmarks export \-\-format=netscape \\
    \-\-output ./bookmarks.html
.fi
.RE

.TP
.B Dedupe with a conflict report, then apply
.PP
.RS
.nf
linkmarks dedupe              # dry-run; review the report
linkmarks dedupe \-\-apply     # commit the canonical set
.fi
.RE

.TP
.B Launch the interactive terminal browser
.PP
.RS
.nf
linkmarks tui
linkmarks tui \-\-source=firefox
.fi
.RE

